<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umbutfo Eswatini Defence Force</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Umbutfo Swaziland Defence Force</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Umbutfo <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Eswatini</a> Defence Force is the army of Eswatini, formed after independence in 1968. Its name, umbutfo, refers to the traditional Swazi age-regiments from which it draws its identity, and the king is its commander-in-chief. A small force, it has been used mainly for border security and internal duties and has never fought a foreign war.</p></div>
